CHANGED: Normalization got faster again: the compile-time reduction of vector primitives dispatches through a map and no longer infers the type of primitives that cannot return a vector, the used arguments of a primitive's blackbox are computed once per primitive instead of at every attempt, recursion checks during inlining no longer descend into types, lifting a binder no longer alpha-compares it against every existing global binder, and the cleanup phase no longer re-runs its flattening strategy on unchanged expressions.
